sentences.l:
There the two took, the one the son of Areithous the lord,
in Arne dwelling, Menesthius, whom the club-wielder
Areithous begot, and Phylomedusa, ox-eyed;

“Let us rouse the strong might of Hector, the horse-taming,
if perhaps some one of the Danaans he will challenge, singly, alone,
in open opposition to fight in fearsome fighting,

So he spoke, and did not disobey, the goddess, gleaming-eyed Athena.
And of them Helenus, Priam’s dear son, put together in spirit
the plan, which pleased the gods as they were devising;

the others make sit, the Trojans and all the Achaeans,
and yourself challenge, of the Achaeans, whoever is best
in open opposition to fight in fearsome fighting;

So he spoke, and Hector in turn rejoiced greatly, the speech having heard,
and going into the middle he held back the battle-lines of the Trojans,
by the middle of his spear having taken hold;
